# ==============================================================================
# Target configuration for dev-sync.
# Format: <target_name>=<raw_local>|<remote_path>
#
# Supported dynamic variables:
#   $LOCAL_BASE : Automatically resolves to the parent directory of dev-sync
#                 (e.g. C:\dev on Windows, $HOME/dev on macOS/Linux/Android)
#                 or can be overridden with the DEV_SYNC_BASE environment variable.
#   $HOME       : Resolves to the user's home directory across all platforms.
#   $ANY_VAR    : Any active system environment variable (e.g. $WORKSPACE).
#
# Supported remote backends:
#   Any rclone-supported remote: Google Drive (gdrive:), AWS S3 (s3:),
#   OneDrive (onedrive:), Dropbox, SFTP (sftp:), or local paths.
# ==============================================================================

# Standard development workspaces
projects=$LOCAL_BASE/projects|gdrive:projects
phone_projects=$LOCAL_BASE/phone_projects|gdrive:phone_projects

# Example of targeting user home directory:
# docs=$HOME/Documents/dev-notes|gdrive:backup/notes

# Example of targeting AWS S3 or compatible object storage:
# cloud_data=$LOCAL_BASE/datasets|s3:my-bucket/datasets
